    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMiniJump2D\n\n### Description\n\nApologies if this is possible and I'm not seeing how to do it: can I set up more than one jumping command with mini jump2d?\r\n\r\nThat is, I want to do something like\r\n```lua\r\nmini_jump2d.setup({\r\nspotter = mini_jump2d.gen_pattern_spotter(\"pattern_s\"), \r\n...,\r\nmappings = {\r\nstart_jumping = \"s\",\r\n}\r\n)\r\n```\r\nand then also\r\n```lua\r\nmini_jump2d.setup({\r\nspotter = mini_jump2d.gen_pattern_spotter(\"pattern_S\"), \r\n...,\r\nmappings = {\r\nstart_jumping = \"S\",\r\n}\r\n)\r\n```\r\nso that I can use `s` and `S`, say, to jump to two different patterns. When I try the above, both `s` and `S` use only the `pattern_S` pattern, rather than `pattern_s` and `pattern_S`, respectively.",
