            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No worries!\r\n\r\n'mini.jump2d' exports [`start()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8e18eb9ba849d737acac1873cd78fc8058c1700a/doc/mini-jump2d.txt#L255) function which can be used with different options inside custom mappings. Here are [examples of how it can be called](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8e18eb9ba849d737acac1873cd78fc8058c1700a/doc/mini-jump2d.txt#L314-L328).\r\n\r\nHere is an example of how to make mappings like you want (modify to your liking and add them to your config to make more persistent):\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', 'S', function() MiniJump2d.start({ spotter = MiniJump2d.gen_pattern_spotter('%S+') }) end)\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', 's', function() MiniJump2d.start({ spotter = MiniJump2d.gen_pattern_spotter('%p') }) end)\r\n```\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nFor the future, [Q&A discussions](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/categories/q-a) is a better place to ask questions.",
